| `agents/practice_refactor/` | Refactors code toward one named practice, a corpus neighbourhood at a time, gating every edit on `make verify`. Unreadable walk, baseline and apply reports raise the shared `ToolReportUnreadable`; the CLI reports FAILURE with its three parts, while nonzero queries keep `WalkRefused` and USAGE. | `python3 scripts/refactor_practice.py` | [a practice's `id`](settings.md#configpracticesjson), [`corpus.served_visibilities`](settings.md#configprojectjson) | One practice per run; it cannot mark a chunk done while the gate is red. The walk and proposal use the served levels of the checkout whose corpus is read. A chunk at a level outside the served levels, in the corpus or in what its file states on disk now, is no candidate and never reaches a prompt; a chunk whose file's level cannot be read is no candidate either. | [coding-practices.md](../guides/coding-practices.md) | always |
